# Shell scripts must be checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# The blobs in this repo are LF. The problem is checkout: with core.autocrlf=true
# (the Windows default, and what this project's Windows clones use) git smudges
# them to CRLF on the way out, and that breaks
# scripts/push-migrations-selfhosted.sh in a way that is not obvious from reading
# it. Bash matches a quoted here-doc terminator literally, so `SQL\r` does not
# close a block opened with <<'SQL': the here-doc runs to end of file, swallowing
# the rest of the script. The migration runner then feeds its own source to psql
# instead of the history-table DDL, reports "FATAL: could not create history
# table", and exits before applying anything.
#
# --dry-run skips that here-doc, so the script looks healthy right up until the
# moment it is used for real.
#
# eol=lf overrides autocrlf per file, so a Windows checkout gets LF here while
# everything else keeps the existing behaviour. Deliberately narrow: a repo-wide
# `* text=auto` would renormalise every file and bury this in the churn.
*.sh text eol=lf
